        "question": "Can a GovernLoom policy prevent a Python tool side effect, and what must the developer integrate?",
        "status": "returned",
        "answer": {
          "answer": "Yes\u2014if the developer integrates RuntimeHook.wrap_tool at the actual side-effect boundary and uses enforce mode. It sends a tool event before invocation; an input block raises PolicyViolation and prevents the target call. Output monitoring cannot undo side effects that already occurred. The developer must activate a policy, supply a scoped server-side ingestion key, wrap the actual tool callable, and handle PolicyViolation for fallback or review. Flag/review actions require their own handling; a collector decision alone does not prove client enforcement.",
